WEBVTT

00:00:58.471 --> 00:01:01.015
James Dyke: The concern
that I’ve got about net zero,

00:01:01.015 --> 00:01:03.309
you're probably going to
disagree about this,

00:01:03.351 --> 00:01:06.395
it might be taking away some
of the sense of urgency.

00:01:06.437 --> 00:01:08.815
JF: We can be optimistic
or we can be pessimistic.

00:01:08.856 --> 00:01:10.316
But the work looks the same.

00:01:10.316 --> 00:01:13.111
Is there anything that struck you
about carbon credits

00:01:13.111 --> 00:01:15.279
or carbon markets
that you want to talk about?

00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:17.448
AG: Well, I'll wait
until the session is over

00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:19.617
to give us some considered
opinions on that.

00:01:20.785 --> 00:01:26.666
[TED Countdown Dilemma Series]

